NAME
    net - network status and trust management

SYNOPSIS
    net
    net scan | discover | peers
    net trust <addr> [full]
    net block <addr>
    net revoke <addr>
    net send <addr> <message>

DESCRIPTION
    net is the front end to TOS's zero-trust networking. With no argument it
    shows status (address, hostname, port, peer counts). Trust changes require an
    ADMIN session and are always a deliberate local action.

SUBCOMMANDS
    (none)              Show network status.
    scan / discover     Broadcast a ping and collect responding peers.
    peers / list        List known peers with their trust level.
    trust <addr>        Raise a peer to KNOWN.
    trust <addr> full   Raise a peer to TRUSTED (enables encrypted messaging,
                        file transfer, and remote execution with that peer).
    block <addr>        Drop all packets from a peer.
    revoke <addr>       Reset a peer to UNKNOWN.
    send <addr> <msg>   Send an encrypted message to a TRUSTED peer.

EXAMPLES
    net scan
    net trust 3f8a1c2d full
    net send 3f8a1c2d "build complete"

SEE ALSO
    man networking, ping, chat, rsh, scp, MANUAL.md (Chapter 8)
